#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pi-employee: the per-employee Pi launcher (sf#1493 P0.3). Paperclip's
pi_local adapter runs it as its `command` in place of `pi`; it fits the run to
the seat named by FLEET_EMPLOYEE, then execs the real pi.

Usage: pi-employee <pi argv...>   (exactly what the adapter would pass to pi)

Fleet root: env PI_EMPLOYEE_FLEET_ROOT, else the parent of this script's
directory (~/fleet on a box, fleet/ in the repo).

0. Every invocation loads the fleet-wide live-catalog extension
   <root>/pi-extensions/fleet-proxy-models/index.ts (registers `fleet-proxy`
   from GET /v1/models on each Pi start; no seat models file). Missing: exit 3.
1. argv holding --version, -v, --help or -h: exec pi with argv and env
   unchanged. --list-models (Paperclip's model check) execs pi with
   `-ne -e <live-catalog ext>` prepended and env unchanged; no profile is read.
2. Otherwise FLEET_EMPLOYEE (lowercased, ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$) names the seat and
   <root>/pi/profiles/<seat>.json is its profile (v0: tools, extensions,
   agentDir; see fleet/pi/profiles/README.md). Every extension must exist, and
   `pi --version` must match the pin in <root>/pi/versions.json.
3. argv is rewritten: every --tools value becomes the profile's tools (one
   --tools is added at the front when absent), and `-ne` then `-e <abs path>`
   per extension go first, the live-catalog extension before the profile's.
   Everything else keeps its order; the prompt stays last.
   PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR is set to the seat's agentDir (created, mode 700), and
   TMPDIR, TMP and TEMP to <agentDir>/tmp (created, mode 700), overriding the
   caller's. An agentDir or temp dir resolving (realpath) to or under
   /tmp, /private/tmp or /var/tmp is refused before anything is created.
   <agentDir>/settings.json, when absent, is written as the cheapest Pi
   compaction (COMPACTION below: keep 4k recent tokens); an existing file is
   left untouched.
   FLEET_MODEL and FLEET_EFFORT are set from argv, overriding the caller's
   (sf#1930): FLEET_MODEL is the --model value without a `fleet-proxy/`
   prefix or a `:<level>` suffix, FLEET_EFFORT the --thinking value (else that
   suffix), so forge-post's run evidence names what this run uses. Absent
   from argv: the caller's value stays.
4. A run whose argv carries `--mode json` (or `--mode=json`) runs pi as a
   child with its stdout piped through pi-stdout-filter, found next to this
   script (sf#1602): Paperclip keeps only the events its parsers read. stdin
   and stderr pass straight through. Filter missing or not startable: one
   stderr warning, then the unfiltered exec. Any other run execs pi.
5. A filtered run stops everything it started, and nothing else (sf#2001).
   Stop causes: SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP to this launcher (never forwarded;
   the first one wins), a disconnect (POLLHUP or POLLERR on fd 1, polled once
   a second with the mask POLLHUP; fd 0 is at end-of-file in normal operation
   and is never polled), and a filter that exits non-zero while pi runs. A
   cause is seen at the next one-second tick. What the run started is what
   this launcher recorded:
   - pi runs as the leader of its own process group, which is signalled only
     while pi is unreaped. Hand-run on a terminal, pi is therefore in a
     background group, and a pi that reads the terminal is stopped by SIGTTIN.
   - a ledger of pi's descendants as (pid, start time), taken from one process
     listing at pi's start and on every tick, so a child that left the group,
     changed directory or lost its parent is still known. While pi is
     unreaped every listing also records the members of pi's group, and a
     tick lists before it reaps, so a pi that exited between two ticks leaves
     its group recorded.
   - at stop time only, and relied on for nothing: processes of this uid whose
     environment holds PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID=<this run> (not readable for an Apple
     system binary), and the run's callback bridge, trusted only when
     $PAPERCLIP_BRIDGE_QUEUE_DIR/server.pid names a process of this uid whose
     argv holds both paperclip-bridge-server.mjs and
     /.paperclip-runtime/runs/<this run>/; a pid file that is not 1 to 10
     ASCII digits is not trusted. Both need a PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID matching
     [A-Za-z0-9_-]+; without one the last line ends `; no run id`.
   Only processes of this uid are signalled, and never this launcher, its
   parent, pid 1 or any pid on this launcher's parent chain in the listing at
   hand: none of them is adopted from any source, and no walk descends from
   one, so a wrapper above the launcher that carries the run id is left
   alone. The stop: SIGTERM to the group and the ledger, a grace, SIGKILL to
   the group, then the same for what is left by pid; a trusted bridge's pid
   file is unlinked once the bridge is gone. The grace is 5 s (env
   PI_EMPLOYEE_STOP_GRACE, seconds, for tests) and the whole stop has one
   deadline, 2 x grace + 4 s: 14 s, plus the tick before it, against the
   adapter's 20 s SIGKILL of a locally run launcher. Every listing, finder
   and wait of the stop checks the deadline first, and a listing's timeout is
   the lesser of 1 s and the time left. Once the deadline has passed, or a
   step raised an unexpected error, no new listing is taken: the final
   SIGKILLs go to the group and, by pid, to the rows of the last successful
   listing, so the stop ends within the deadline plus about 2.5 s (one
   listing in flight, the count listing, the filter wait).
   When a listing of the stop fails, signals by pid go to the ledger as last
   confirmed only if the last successful listing was at most 10 s before the
   stop began; older than that, nothing is signalled by pid. Within that
   window a recorded pid is signalled on the strength of signal 0 alone; a
   stranger would need the pid reused inside those seconds.
   Then one stderr line, written without blocking,
   `pi-employee: stopped on <cause>; <n> run processes stopped`, followed when
   true by `; <m> still alive`, `; no run id`, `; listing failed`.
   When pi has exited and the filter has not, the launcher waits up to 0.5 s
   for the filter, then keeps ticking until the filter is done; a stop cause
   then stops the ledger by pid only.
   Not stopped: (1) a process that left pi's group and whose whole ancestry
   died inside one tick before a walk saw it; (2) a child forked between the
   last listing and the kill of its parent. A run that is exec'ed (no
   `--mode json`, or the filter did not start) has none of this.
   Limits: every process lookup has a timeout of 1 s or less. Linux /proc
   enumeration and reads share one alarm deadline; an expired lookup returns
   no partial data. A kernel operation that cannot be interrupted, or a `ps`
   process that cannot be killed, can still exceed that budget.

pi: env PI_EMPLOYEE_PI_BIN, else `pi` on PATH. No network. The prompt and env
values are never printed.

Exit: whatever pi exits (exec, or pi's own code or signal when filtered);
3 refused (bad seat, profile, extension, version or OS temp dir), one
`pi-employee: ...` line on stderr; after a stop, 128 + the signal (143, 130,
129), or 1 for a disconnect or a failed filter.
"""
from contextlib import contextmanager
import json
import os
import re
import select
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

FILTER = "pi-stdout-filter"
GRACE = 5.0
RUN_ID_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+")
PID_FILE_RE = re.compile(r"[0-9]{1,10}")
# A failed stop listing falls back to the recorded pids only this fresh.
FALLBACK_AGE = 10.0
BRIDGE_ENTRY = "paperclip-bridge-server.mjs"
LINUX = sys.platform.startswith("linux")
# One listing row: parent pid, process group, uid, state, start time.
PPID, PGID, UID, STAT, START = range(5)
PIN_KEY = "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent"
PASSTHROUGH = {"--list-models", "--version", "-v", "--help", "-h"}
MODELS_EXT = os.path.join("pi-extensions", "fleet-proxy-models", "index.ts")
SEAT_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$")
TOOL_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$")
OS_TMP = ("/tmp", "/private/tmp", "/var/tmp", "/private/var/tmp")
# Pi settings a seat gets when its agentDir has none. Paperclip already starts a
# fresh session each run (agents.json sessionCompaction), so compaction only
# fires inside one long run; keeping 4k recent tokens is the cheap part.
COMPACTION = {"compaction": {"enabled": True, "reserveTokens": 16384, "keepRecentTokens": 4000}}


def refuse(msg):
    sys.stderr.write("pi-employee: %s\n" % msg)
    sys.exit(3)


def not_os_tmp(path):
    real = os.path.realpath(path)
    for banned in OS_TMP:
        if os.path.commonpath([real, banned]) == banned:
            refuse("%s resolves to %s, under %s: seat temp never lives in "
                   "the OS temp dir" % (path, real, banned))


def load_profile(root, seat):
    path = os.path.join(root, "pi", "profiles", seat + ".json")

    def bad(what):
        refuse("profile %s: %s" % (path, what))

    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            data = json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        bad("not found")
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        bad("unreadable: %s" % type(e).__name__)
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        bad("not a JSON object")
    tools = data.get("tools")
    if not isinstance(tools, list) or not tools:
        bad("tools must be a non-empty list")
    for t in tools:
        if not isinstance(t, str) or not TOOL_RE.match(t):
            bad("tools: bad tool name")
    exts = data.get("extensions")
    if not isinstance(exts, list) or not all(isinstance(e, str) and e for e in exts):
        bad("extensions must be a list of paths")
    agent_dir = data.get("agentDir", "~/.pi/seats/" + seat)
    if not isinstance(agent_dir, str) or not agent_dir:
        bad("agentDir must be a string")
    return tools, exts, os.path.expanduser(agent_dir)


def pinned(root):
    path = os.path.join(root, "pi", "versions.json")
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            want = json.load(f)[PIN_KEY]
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        refuse("versions %s: no %s pin" % (path, PIN_KEY))
    return want


def installed(pi):
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(
            [pi, "--version"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30
        ).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return "<none>"
    tokens = out.split()
    return tokens[-1] if tokens else "<none>"


def rewrite(argv, tools, ext_paths):
    tool_list = ",".join(tools)
    out = []
    seen = False
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a == "--tools" and i + 1 < len(argv):
            out += ["--tools", tool_list]
            seen = True
            i += 2
            continue
        if a.startswith("--tools="):
            out.append("--tools=" + tool_list)
            seen = True
        else:
            out.append(a)
        i += 1
    head = ["-ne"]
    for p in ext_paths:
        head += ["-e", p]
    if not seen:
        head += ["--tools", tool_list]
    return head + out


def main():
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    pi = os.environ.get("PI_EMPLOYEE_PI_BIN") or "pi"
    root = os.environ.get("PI_EMPLOYEE_FLEET_ROOT") or os.path.dirname(
        os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
    )
    if any(a in PASSTHROUGH for a in argv) and "--list-models" not in argv:
        os.execvpe(pi, [pi] + argv, os.environ)
    models_ext = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(root, MODELS_EXT))
    if not os.path.exists(models_ext):
        refuse("extension not found: %s" % models_ext)
    if "--list-models" in argv:
        os.execvpe(pi, [pi, "-ne", "-e", models_ext] + argv, os.environ)

    seat = (os.environ.get("FLEET_EMPLOYEE") or "").lower()
    if not SEAT_RE.match(seat):
        refuse("FLEET_EMPLOYEE is missing or not a seat name")

    tools, exts, agent_dir = load_profile(root, seat)
    not_os_tmp(agent_dir)
    not_os_tmp(os.path.join(agent_dir, "tmp"))
    ext_paths = [models_ext]
    for e in exts:
        p = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(root, os.path.expanduser(e)))
        if not os.path.exists(p):
            refuse("extension not found: %s" % p)
        ext_paths.append(p)

    want = pinned(root)
    got = installed(pi)
    if got != want:
        refuse("pi %s installed, fleet pins %s" % (got, want))

    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR"] = agent_dir
    os.makedirs(agent_dir, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    write_default_settings(agent_dir)
    seat_tmp = os.path.join(agent_dir, "tmp")
    os.makedirs(seat_tmp, exist_ok=True)
    not_os_tmp(seat_tmp)
    os.chmod(seat_tmp, 0o700)
    env["TMPDIR"] = env["TMP"] = env["TEMP"] = seat_tmp
    env.update(run_model(argv))
    cmd = [pi] + rewrite(argv, tools, ext_paths)
    if json_mode(argv):
        run_filtered(cmd, env)
    os.execvpe(pi, cmd, env)


def write_default_settings(agent_dir):
    """Create <agentDir>/settings.json with COMPACTION; never replace one."""
    final = os.path.join(agent_dir, "settings.json")
    tmp = final + ".tmp.%s" % os.getpid()
    try:
        with open(tmp, "x", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            json.dump(COMPACTION, f)
            f.write("\n")
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        try:
            os.link(tmp, final)
        except FileExistsError:
            pass
    finally:
        os.unlink(tmp)


def flag(argv, name):
    """The last value of `name` in argv, as `name v` or `name=v`, else None."""
    val = None
    for i, a in enumerate(argv):
        if a == name and i + 1 < len(argv):
            val = argv[i + 1]
        elif a.startswith(name + "="):
            val = a[len(name) + 1:]
    return val


def run_model(argv):
    """FLEET_MODEL and FLEET_EFFORT as this run's argv names them (sf#1930)."""
    out = {}
    model = flag(argv, "--model")
    effort = flag(argv, "--thinking")
    if model:
        model, _, level = model.partition(":")
        if model.startswith("fleet-proxy/"):
            model = model[len("fleet-proxy/"):]
        out["FLEET_MODEL"] = model
        effort = effort or level
        # A run that names its model but no level must not inherit a stale one.
        out["FLEET_EFFORT"] = effort
    elif effort:
        out["FLEET_EFFORT"] = effort
    return out


def json_mode(argv):
    return "--mode=json" in argv or any(
        a == "--mode" and b == "json" for a, b in zip(argv, argv[1:])
    )


def stop_grace():
    try:
        grace = float(os.environ.get("PI_EMPLOYEE_STOP_GRACE", ""))
    except ValueError:
        return GRACE
    return grace if 0 < grace < float("inf") else GRACE


def run_ps(args, timeout=1.0):
    """Text of one /bin/ps call, or None when it failed or outlived `timeout`
    (1 s at most)."""
    env = dict(os.environ, LC_ALL="C", TZ="UTC")
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["/bin/ps"] + args, capture_output=True,
                             timeout=timeout, env=env)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    if out.returncode != 0:
        return None
    return out.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace")


class ProcTimeout(Exception):
    """The Linux process reader exhausted its total budget."""


@contextmanager
def proc_budget(timeout):
    """Bound even a blocked proc read. The launcher is single-threaded.

    Never leave our alarm installed or restart a caller's timer from scratch.
    ProcTimeout is deliberately not one of the per-pid, skippable errors.
    """
    if timeout <= 0:
        raise ProcTimeout()

    def expired(_signum, _frame):
        raise ProcTimeout()

    previous_handler = signal.getsignal(signal.SIGALRM)
    started = time.monotonic()
    previous_timer = signal.getitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL)
    if previous_timer[0] and previous_timer[0] <= timeout:
        # A shorter caller-owned deadline wins; do not replace or defer it.
        raise ProcTimeout()
    signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, expired)
    try:
        signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, timeout)
        yield
    finally:
        try:
            signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, 0)
        finally:
            # Expiry during disarm must still restore the caller's state.
            signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, previous_handler)
            delay, interval = previous_timer
            if delay:
                delay = max(0.000001, delay - (time.monotonic() - started))
            signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, delay, interval)


def linux_stat(pid):
    """(ppid, pgid, state, starttime) from /proc/<pid>/stat; raises if gone."""
    with open("/proc/%d/stat" % pid, "rb") as f:
        # The command name may hold spaces and brackets: split after the LAST ")".
        tail = f.read().rsplit(b")", 1)[1].split()
    state = tail[0].decode("ascii", "replace")
    return int(tail[1]), int(tail[2]), state, int(tail[19])


def linux_uid(pid):
    with open("/proc/%d/status" % pid, "rb") as f:
        for line in f:
            if line.startswith(b"Uid:"):
                return int(line.split()[1])
    raise ValueError("no Uid line")


def linux_pids():
    return [int(name) for name in os.listdir("/proc") if name.isdigit()]


def list_procs(timeout=1.0):
    """Every process as {pid: (ppid, pgid, uid, state, start time)}, or None
    when the listing failed. A start time is only ever compared for equality
    with another one from this function (or from env_matches)."""
    rows = {}
    if LINUX:
        try:
            with proc_budget(timeout):
                for pid in linux_pids():
                    try:
                        ppid, pgid, state, start = linux_stat(pid)
                        rows[pid] = (ppid, pgid, linux_uid(pid), state, start)
                    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
                        continue
        except (OSError, ProcTimeout):
            return None
    else:
        # One -o per column; lstart is last because it holds spaces. LC_ALL=C
        # and TZ=UTC keep it the same string for the same process all run long.
        text = run_ps(["-A", "-o", "pid=", "-o", "ppid=", "-o", "pgid=",
                       "-o", "uid=", "-o", "stat=", "-o", "lstart="], timeout)
        if text is None:
            return None
        for line in text.splitlines():
            f = line.split()
            if len(f) != 10:
                continue
            try:
                rows[int(f[0])] = (int(f[1]), int(f[2]), int(f[3]), f[4],
                                   " ".join(f[5:]))
            except ValueError:
                continue
    # A listing without this very process is not a listing.
    return rows if os.getpid() in rows else None


def env_matches(run_id, uid, timeout=1.0):
    """(pid, start time) of every process of `uid` whose environment holds
    PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID=<run_id>, pid and start time from one read; None when the
    read failed. On macOS the text searched is arguments plus environment, and
    an Apple system binary shows no environment at all."""
    token = "PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID=" + run_id
    found = []
    if LINUX:
        try:
            with proc_budget(timeout):
                for pid in linux_pids():
                    try:
                        if linux_uid(pid) != uid:
                            continue
                        start = linux_stat(pid)[3]
                        with open("/proc/%d/environ" % pid, "rb") as f:
                            hit = token.encode() in f.read().split(b"\0")
                        if hit and linux_stat(pid)[3] == start:
                            found.append((pid, start))
                    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
                        continue
        except (OSError, ProcTimeout):
            return None
        return found
    text = run_ps(["-E", "-ww", "-U", str(uid), "-o", "pid=", "-o", "lstart=",
                   "-o", "command="], timeout)
    if text is None:
        return None
    for line in text.splitlines():
        f = line.split(None, 6)
        if len(f) == 7 and f[0].isdigit() and token in f[6].split():
            found.append((int(f[0]), " ".join(f[1:6])))
    return found


def live_argv(pid, timeout=1.0):
    """The live argv of `pid` as one string, or None when it cannot be read."""
    if LINUX:
        try:
            with proc_budget(timeout):
                with open("/proc/%d/cmdline" % pid, "rb") as f:
                    return f.read().replace(b"\0", b" ").decode("utf-8", "replace")
        except (OSError, ProcTimeout):
            return None
    return run_ps(["-ww", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(pid)], timeout)


def send(pid, sig, group=False):
    # On macOS killpg on a group whose only member is the unreaped zombie
    # leader raises PermissionError: the normal case once pi's tree obeyed.
    try:
        (os.killpg if group else os.kill)(pid, sig)
    except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
        pass


class Overrun(Exception):
    """The stop's one deadline passed before its last step."""


class Run:
    """What one filtered run started, and the stop routine (sf#2001)."""

    def __init__(self, pi_pid, flt_pid):
        self.pi = pi_pid
        self.flt = flt_pid
        self.pi_reaped = False
        self.flt_reaped = False
        self.uid = os.getuid()
        # Never adopted, so never signalled: this launcher, its parent, pid 1,
        # and the filter (reaped by its own pid, never counted); every listing
        # adds this launcher's parent chain in it.
        self.fixed = {os.getpid(), os.getppid(), 1, flt_pid}
        self.skip = set(self.fixed)
        self.rows = None  # the last successful listing
        self.rows_at = 0.0  # its monotonic time
        self.entered = 0.0  # monotonic time the stop routine began
        self.ledger = {}  # pid -> (start time, uid)
        self.signalled = set()  # (pid, start time) sent a signal by pid or group
        self.counted = set()  # (pid, start time) of ours seen alive by the stop
        self.grace = stop_grace()
        run_id = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID") or ""
        self.run_id = run_id if RUN_ID_RE.fullmatch(run_id) else None
        self.bridge = None  # (pid, start time, pid file) once trusted
        self.listing_failed = False
        self.deadline = 0.0

    def pi_done(self):
        self.pi_reaped = True
        self.ledger.pop(self.pi, None)

    def reap(self, pid):
        """True once `pid` (pi or the filter) is reaped; each is reaped once."""
        if pid == self.pi and self.pi_reaped or pid == self.flt and self.flt_reaped:
            return True
        try:
            done = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)[0]
        except ChildProcessError:
            done = pid
        if done and pid == self.pi:
            self.pi_done()
        elif done:
            self.flt_reaped = True
        return bool(done)

    def walk(self, rows):
        """Confirm the ledger against one listing, then adopt pi and every
        member of its group of this uid (while pi is unreaped), then every
        descendant of each entry, to any depth. First the listing is recorded
        and this launcher's parent chain in it joins the never-signalled set:
        a wrapper above the launcher can carry the run id."""
        self.rows, self.rows_at = rows, time.monotonic()
        chain = set()
        pid = os.getpid()
        while pid > 1 and pid in rows and pid not in chain:
            chain.add(pid)
            pid = rows[pid][PPID]
        self.skip = self.fixed | chain
        for pid in list(self.ledger):
            row = rows.get(pid)
            # Gone, or a stranger now holds the pid: its children are not ours.
            if (row is None or row[START] != self.ledger[pid][0]
                    or pid in self.skip):
                del self.ledger[pid]
        if not self.pi_reaped:
            # An unreaped pi, zombie included, still owns its pid, so the group
            # id is safe to read. A dead pi's children have parent pid 1: the
            # group is the only thing that still ties them to the run.
            for pid, row in rows.items():
                if pid == self.pi or (row[PGID] == self.pi
                                      and row[UID] == self.uid
                                      and pid not in self.skip):
                    self.ledger.setdefault(pid, (row[START], row[UID]))
        kids = {}
        for pid, row in rows.items():
            kids.setdefault(row[PPID], []).append(pid)
        todo = list(self.ledger)
        while todo:
            for pid in kids.get(todo.pop(), ()):
                if pid in self.ledger or pid in self.skip:
                    continue
                # A row of another uid is adopted (its children may be the
                # run's) and is never signalled or counted.
                self.ledger[pid] = (rows[pid][START], rows[pid][UID])
                todo.append(pid)

    def tick_walk(self):
        rows = list_procs()
        if rows is not None:
            self.walk(rows)

    def left(self):
        """Seconds to the stop's deadline; raises once it has passed."""
        left = self.deadline - time.monotonic()
        if left <= 0:
            raise Overrun()
        return left

    def look(self):
        """One stop-routine listing: walked, and what is ours and alive
        counted. The deadline is checked first, the timeout is the lesser of
        1 s and the time left, and a failed listing is retried once when at
        least 1 s is left. None when it failed; the ledger then stays as last
        confirmed."""
        rows = list_procs(min(1.0, self.left()))
        if rows is None and self.left() >= 1:
            rows = list_procs()
        if rows is None:
            self.listing_failed = True
        else:
            self.walk(rows)
        self.count(rows)
        return rows

    def live(self, rows):
        """Ledger pids of this uid that are alive: in `rows` with the recorded
        start time and not a zombie. With no listing, every entry that answers
        signal 0, start time unchecked, and none at all when the last
        successful listing is too old to stand on."""
        out = []
        if rows is None and not self.fallback_ok():
            return out
        for pid, (start, uid) in self.ledger.items():
            if uid != self.uid or pid in self.skip:
                continue
            if rows is None:
                try:
                    os.kill(pid, 0)
                except OSError:
                    continue
            elif (pid not in rows or rows[pid][START] != start
                  or rows[pid][STAT].startswith("Z")):
                continue
            out.append(pid)
        return out

    def fallback_ok(self):
        """The last successful listing was at most FALLBACK_AGE before the
        stop routine began (any listing of the stop itself is)."""
        return (self.rows is not None
                and self.rows_at >= self.entered - FALLBACK_AGE)

    def count(self, rows):
        for pid in self.live(rows):
            self.counted.add((pid, self.ledger[pid][0]))

    def signal(self, rows, sig, fresh=False, group_sent=False):
        """`sig` by pid to every live entry; only the not yet signalled ones
        when `fresh`; `group_sent` marks pi's group as already signalled."""
        for pid in self.live(rows):
            key = (pid, self.ledger[pid][0])
            if fresh and key in self.signalled:
                continue
            self.signalled.add(key)
            in_group = pid == self.pi or (rows is not None
                                          and rows[pid][PGID] == self.pi)
            if not (group_sent and in_group):
                send(pid, sig)

    def pause(self, end, step=0.5):
        """Sleep one step toward `end`; False once `end` has passed."""
        left = self.left()
        now = time.monotonic()
        if now >= end:
            return False
        time.sleep(min(step, end - now, left))
        return True

    def group_quiet(self, rows):
        """pi is a zombie or absent and no member of its group is alive."""
        if rows is None:
            return False
        return not any(
            not row[STAT].startswith("Z")
            for pid, row in rows.items()
            if pid == self.pi or row[PGID] == self.pi
        )

    def adopt_by_id(self, rows):
        """The environment matches and the bridge; both need the run id."""
        if self.run_id is None:
            return
        found = env_matches(self.run_id, self.uid, min(1.0, self.left()))
        if found is None:
            self.listing_failed = True
        for pid, start in found or ():
            if pid not in self.skip:
                self.ledger.setdefault(pid, (start, self.uid))
        queue = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_BRIDGE_QUEUE_DIR")
        if not queue or rows is None:
            return
        pid_file = queue + "/server.pid"
        self.left()
        try:
            with open(pid_file, encoding="ascii") as f:
                text = f.read().strip()
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return
        pid = int(text) if PID_FILE_RE.fullmatch(text) else 0
        row = rows.get(pid)
        if pid <= 0 or pid in self.skip or row is None or row[UID] != self.uid:
            return
        argv = live_argv(pid, min(1.0, self.left()))
        if argv is None:
            self.listing_failed = True
        elif (BRIDGE_ENTRY in argv
              and "/.paperclip-runtime/runs/%s/" % self.run_id in argv):
            self.ledger.setdefault(pid, (row[START], row[UID]))
            self.bridge = (pid, row[START], pid_file)

    def stop(self, cause, code):
        """Stop the group, the ledger and the bridge inside one deadline,
        report one line, exit `code`. Never returns."""
        self.entered = time.monotonic()
        self.deadline = self.entered + 2 * self.grace + 4
        try:
            if not self.pi_reaped:
                self.stop_group()
            self.stop_ledger()
        except Exception:
            # The deadline passed (Overrun) or a step failed: no new listing.
            # The final kills go from the last successful one, if it is fresh
            # enough to stand on.
            try:
                rows = self.rows if self.fallback_ok() else None
                if not self.pi_reaped:
                    send(self.pi, signal.SIGKILL, group=True)
                self.count(rows)
                self.signal(rows, signal.SIGKILL)
            except Exception:
                pass
        try:
            self.finish(cause, code)
        except Exception:
            pass
        sys.exit(code)

    def stop_group(self):
        """Steps 1 to 4. pi is unreaped throughout, so its pid, which is the
        group id, cannot have been given to another process."""
        rows = self.look()
        send(self.pi, signal.SIGTERM, group=True)
        self.signal(rows, signal.SIGTERM, group_sent=True)
        end = time.monotonic() + self.grace
        while not self.group_quiet(rows) and self.pause(end):
            rows = self.look()
            self.signal(rows, signal.SIGTERM, fresh=True)
        self.look()
        # The last signal the group gets, unless the deadline passes.
        send(self.pi, signal.SIGKILL, group=True)
        end = time.monotonic() + 2
        while not self.reap(self.pi) and self.pause(end, 0.1):
            pass

    def stop_ledger(self):
        """Steps 5 to 7: what is left, by pid."""
        rows = self.look()
        self.adopt_by_id(rows)
        self.count(rows)
        self.signal(rows, signal.SIGTERM)
        end = time.monotonic() + self.grace
        while self.live(rows) and self.pause(end):
            rows = self.look()
            self.signal(rows, signal.SIGTERM, fresh=True)
        rows = self.look()
        self.signal(rows, signal.SIGKILL)
        end = time.monotonic() + 2
        while self.live(rows) and self.pause(end):
            rows = self.look()

    def finish(self, cause, code):
        """The filter, then step 8: count, unlink, one line, exit."""
        # The filter ends on its own once pi's pipe closes; give it the time
        # left to the deadline (0.5 s once that has passed), then kill it.
        end = max(self.deadline, time.monotonic() + 0.5)
        while not self.reap(self.flt) and time.monotonic() < end:
            time.sleep(0.05)
        if not self.flt_reaped:
            send(self.flt, signal.SIGKILL)
            try:
                os.waitpid(self.flt, 0)
            except ChildProcessError:
                pass
            self.flt_reaped = True
        alive = 0 if self.reap(self.pi) else 1
        # One listing, never retried: the deadline may already have passed.
        rows = list_procs()
        if rows is None:
            self.listing_failed = True

        def still(pid, start):
            if rows is None:
                try:
                    os.kill(pid, 0)
                except OSError:
                    return False
                return True
            row = rows.get(pid)
            return bool(row and row[START] == start
                        and not row[STAT].startswith("Z"))

        alive += sum(1 for pid, start in self.counted
                     if pid != self.pi and still(pid, start))
        if self.bridge and rows is not None and not still(*self.bridge[:2]):
            # The adapter's later stop signals whatever pid this file names.
            try:
                os.unlink(self.bridge[2])
            except OSError:
                pass
        line = "pi-employee: stopped on %s; %d run processes stopped" % (
            cause, len(self.counted))
        if alive:
            line += "; %d still alive" % alive
        if self.run_id is None:
            line += "; no run id"
        if self.listing_failed:
            line += "; listing failed"
        # After a disconnect fd 2 is gone too: neither this write nor the
        # interpreter's flush at exit may replace the exit code. Non-blocking,
        # so a full pipe whose reader stopped reading raises instead of
        # holding the launcher; the flag is on the shared open file, so it is
        # put back.
        try:
            blocking = os.get_blocking(2)
            os.set_blocking(2, False)
            try:
                os.write(2, (line + "\n").encode())
            finally:
                os.set_blocking(2, blocking)
        except OSError:
            pass
        try:
            os.dup2(os.open(os.devnull, os.O_WRONLY), 2)
        except OSError:
            pass
        sys.exit(code)


def run_filtered(cmd, env):
    """Run pi with its stdout piped through pi-stdout-filter (sf#1602), and
    stop everything the run started on a stop cause (sf#2001)."""
    filt = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), FILTER)
    # An inherited SIG_IGN would let the kernel reap pi and the filter itself.
    signal.signal(signal.SIGCHLD, signal.SIG_DFL)
    r, w = os.pipe()
    try:
        flt = subprocess.Popen([filt], stdin=r)
    except OSError as e:
        os.close(r)
        os.close(w)
        sys.stderr.write("pi-employee: %s did not start (%s); Pi stream "
                         "unfiltered\n" % (filt, type(e).__name__))
        return
    os.close(r)
    got = []

    def note(sig, _frame):
        # The first cause wins. Nothing is signalled from here: pi is not in
        # this launcher's group, and the stop routine is the only path to it.
        if not got:
            got.append(sig)

    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(sig, note)
    try:
        # Keep the Popen object: a discarded one can be polled (reaped) by
        # subprocess's own cleanup, leaving os.kill/os.waitpid a dead pid.
        # preexec_fn, not process_group: any Python 3, and no threads here.
        pi = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=w, env=env, preexec_fn=os.setpgrp)
    finally:
        os.close(w)
    run = Run(pi.pid, flt.pid)
    run.tick_walk()
    # Mask POLLHUP: an empty mask reports nothing at all on macOS, and
    # POLLOUT would make a healthy pipe always ready.
    poller = select.poll()
    poller.register(1, select.POLLHUP)
    status = 0
    while not (run.pi_reaped and run.flt_reaped):
        cause = None
        if poller is None:
            time.sleep(1)
        else:
            # A returning signal handler does not cut this wait short.
            try:
                events = poller.poll(1000)
            except OSError:
                events = [(1, select.POLLNVAL)]
            for _fd, event in events:
                if event & (select.POLLHUP | select.POLLERR):
                    cause = ("disconnect", 1)
                else:
                    # /dev/null answers POLLNVAL at once: stop polling fd 1
                    # for the rest of the run, or this loop would spin.
                    poller = None
        if got:
            cause = (signal.Signals(got[0]).name, 128 + got[0])
        if cause:
            # Before any reap, so pi is unreaped when its group is signalled.
            run.stop(*cause)
        # Before the reap too: a pi that exited since the last tick is still
        # an unreaped zombie here, and this walk records its group.
        run.tick_walk()
        failed = None
        pi_was_reaped = run.pi_reaped
        while True:
            try:
                pid, st = os.waitpid(-1, os.WNOHANG)
            except ChildProcessError:
                break
            if pid == 0:
                break
            code = os.waitstatus_to_exitcode(st)
            if pid == pi.pid:
                run.pi_done()
                status = code
            elif pid == flt.pid:
                run.flt_reaped = True
                # The filter exits 0 at EOF, which pi reaches by closing
                # stdout or exiting; either way pi's run is intact.
                if code != 0:
                    failed = code
        if failed is not None and not run.pi_reaped:
            run.stop("%s exited %d" % (FILTER, failed), 1)
        if run.pi_reaped and not pi_was_reaped:
            # A normal end: the filter is done within moments of pi, and the
            # run must not wait a whole tick for it.
            end = time.monotonic() + 0.5
            while not run.reap(flt.pid) and time.monotonic() < end:
                time.sleep(0.05)
    if status < 0:
        signal.signal(-status, signal.SIG_DFL)
        os.kill(os.getpid(), -status)
    sys.exit(status if status >= 0 else 128 - status)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
